Two repairs to eqy_partition.cc that make whole-core designs reachable.

Apply against the eqy pinned in configs/pins.env:

    cd thirdparty/eqy
    git apply -p0 ../../patches/eqy-0001-partition-matrix-and-filename.patch

1. Fragment-Partition-Matrix gated behind ll_want_matrix().
   The matrix is a debug visualisation whose nested loop over
   partitions x fragments issues one log() call per cell,
   unconditionally. Measured on ibex_core (5,261 partitions):
       merge_partitions    3.65s -> 0.019s   (190x)
       full partition step 5.36s -> 1.72s    (3.1x)
   On CVA6 it produced a 2.2 GB log and dominated the run.
   Set LL_EQY_MATRIX=1 to restore the original output.

2. Partition names shortened by ll_safe_partname().
   CVA6's generate-block nesting produces partition names longer
   than the 255-byte filename limit, which aborted the run AFTER
   214,903 partitions had been generated. Names over 100 chars
   become an FNV-1a digest plus a readable tail.
   Measured on CVA6: 74,005 of 280,764 names shortened, with
   zero collisions across all 280,764.

With both applied, CVA6's whole core partitions in 790s yielding
280,764 partitions, where it previously produced zero in 17m25s.

